 at the same time they're contributing to  the game's prestige and success by  sending a full contingent of athletes  this former canadian olympian says  despite that contradiction the games are  worthwhile the olympics brings everybody  together  uh under a common batter and in a  difficult world that's um  that's a lot better than a kick in the  teeth  and with the performances that we will  see they're going to create moments of  incredible surprise and joy a notable  exception to the diplomatic boycott  russia president vladimir putin took in  the opening festivities a show of  respect to his chinese allies but nbc's  cameras caught putin appearing to doze  off when the team from ukraine entered a  moment that's already generating  intrigue at a time when russian troops  are poised to invade ukraine  saturday marks the first full day of  events and the first awarding of medals  athletes from 91 nations competing  through february 20th it's unclear to  anyone if these olympics will be a  diversion from the pandemic and  international strife or an unwelcome  reminder  ross lord global news  the former wife of jeff bezos mackenzie  scott donated more than 130 million u.s  dollars to a charity supporting  underprivileged students this week her  latest generous donation comes as her  ex-husband is making news in a different  way with his new super yacht as redmond  shannon tells us a famous dutch bridge  is apparently in his way  the historic center of rotterdam was  almost totally destroyed during the nazi  bombing of may 1940  today one of the few landmarks left that  predates the war is this bridge  the distinctive koningshaven to hef to  locals with its rising center trains no  longer use it but it stands as a  towering monument or has until now if it  was just anybody  but this is the world's richest man that  wants to mess with our monument that's  just not okay amazon founder jeff bezos  is reportedly having this super yacht  the largest of its type in the world  built upstream this week it emerged the  bridge will need to be disassembled  temporarily to get bezos's big boat out  to sea i really felt a feeling of  disbelief when i first heard it city  councilor stefan lewis says the plan  must have been known about months ago  before the yacht construction began but  we know that the super yachts are  getting bigger and bigger so are we  going to take this bridge apart every  time such a super yacht needs to pass  through if he likes it  why why not weiner zittleman has written  books about the super rich and our  attitudes toward them i can say the  feeling that someone has about people  like shift basis i can tell you whether  you will be successful or  not successful in life so don't expect  bezos to worry about rubbing up  rotterdam residents the wrong way what  might the neighbor say to this or that i  think this is not the typical question  of successful people the city's mayor  says no permit has been granted for the  bridge work yet bezos would be on the  hook for any associated costs but for a  man worth nearly 200 billion dollars  it's likely to be chump change redmond  shannon global news london  and that is global national for this  friday i'm eric sorenson tonight's your  canada is carbonier newfoundland and  labrador  there are beautiful spots all over  canada email them to viewers at  globalnational.com  thanks for watching  [Applause]  [Music]
 

